1
00:00:01,970 --> 00:00:04,820
If you've got something 
to say, spit it out.

2
00:00:04,820 --> 00:00:07,940
I never said it was taboo, and besides,

3
00:00:07,940 --> 00:00:10,450
I don't like feeling like 
you're tiptoeing around me.

4
00:00:10,450 --> 00:00:13,800
I-It's nothing special.

5
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:15,430
But you said you'd "look into it,"

6
00:00:15,430 --> 00:00:19,540
so why does it feel like getting 
kicked out doesn't bother you at all?

7
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:24,970
D-Don't you feel the least bit sad?

8
00:00:32,890 --> 00:00:33,830
I do.

9
00:00:35,020 --> 00:00:35,920
I do!

10
00:00:38,970 --> 00:00:39,890
And?

11
00:01:20,680 --> 00:01:22,390
I thought I was good at going it alone

12
00:01:20,680 --> 00:01:22,390
Would you prefer to go together?

13
00:01:49,210 --> 00:01:49,920
Place
your finger here

14
00:02:07,980 --> 00:02:11,060
Rent-a-Girlfriend

15
00:02:13,240 --> 00:02:16,910
"Loneliness and Girlfriend"

16
00:02:19,350 --> 00:02:21,460
N-Nothing.

17
00:02:22,370 --> 00:02:23,290
You chicken

18
00:02:22,370 --> 00:02:23,290
Tch.

19
00:02:23,970 --> 00:02:28,750
<i>As if I could say, 
"Sounds like you like me, then"!</i>

20
00:02:25,330 --> 00:02:28,750
Or, "So you're done 
looking into it?"

21
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:32,880
Why don't you live together, then?

22
00:02:34,050 --> 00:02:36,120
Y-Yaemori-san?!

23
00:02:34,470 --> 00:02:37,970
Do you hear yourself?!

24
00:02:35,970 --> 00:02:37,970
Well, if
you're
both
lonely...

25
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:37,970
It's right in front of your eyes.

26
00:02:37,970 --> 00:02:41,420
Mizuhara-san's family home 
should have a spare room or two.

27
00:02:38,010 --> 00:02:44,350
You just said
you had no leads
on a place to live

28
00:02:41,420 --> 00:02:44,350
And sharing a home is the idea 
scenario for your "investigation."

29
00:02:41,560 --> 00:02:44,350
You said so yourself

30
00:02:44,350 --> 00:02:48,310
<i>What is she blurting out? 
How does Mizuhara look?</i>

31
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:48,310
Differing 
opinions...!!

32
00:02:52,940 --> 00:02:54,120
<i>She's red!</i>

33
00:02:54,120 --> 00:02:56,480
<i>Is she blushing, or is it just the booze?</i>

34
00:02:56,480 --> 00:02:58,260
<i>Are you telling me there's a chance?!</i>

35
00:02:57,490 --> 00:02:58,910
Water

36
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:09,710
That idea's so you, Mini-chan. Ridiculous.

37
00:03:10,570 --> 00:03:12,650
That's putting the cart before the horse.

38
00:03:12,650 --> 00:03:15,690
What kind of conclusion is living together 
supposed to help me reach?

39
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:20,070
A boy and girl sharing one roof 
is risky in so many ways.

40
00:03:20,070 --> 00:03:22,560
It's the least logical thing we could do.

41
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:25,520
<i>Trust her to be cool and rational.</i>

42
00:03:25,930 --> 00:03:30,980
<i>Fair. Her feeling lonely is one thing, 
and this is another thing entirely.</i>

43
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:33,940
<i>She doesn't miss me in that way.</i>

44
00:03:33,940 --> 00:03:38,530
You sure? I think it's the best scenario 
to get to know each other better.

45
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:38,530
You're still stuck at that stage?

46
00:03:36,490 --> 00:03:38,530
Don't turn this 
into some in-game event

47
00:03:38,870 --> 00:03:42,300
Heck, how about you two 
just kiss once again?

48
00:03:42,300 --> 00:03:44,540
That should tell you something.

49
00:03:46,430 --> 00:03:48,600
Th-That was a last resort!

50
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:50,230
Yeah, Yaemori-san!

51
00:03:50,230 --> 00:03:53,000
She did that to save my behind!

52
00:03:50,250 --> 00:03:55,300
"That"

53
00:03:50,250 --> 00:03:55,300
Don't get it twisted

54
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:55,300
Whose side are you on, Master?

55
00:03:55,300 --> 00:03:58,130
Ridiculous. That's never happening!

56
00:03:58,470 --> 00:04:00,840
<i>I-It's never happening?</i>

57
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:02,610
Really?

58
00:04:02,610 --> 00:04:03,960
<i>Please stop!</i>

59
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:06,600
<i>We've learned that Mizuhara 
doesn't feel that way at all!</i>

60
00:04:06,600 --> 00:04:10,380
I don't think it's a bad idea to try.

61
00:04:10,380 --> 00:04:14,280
Is the order of things 
really that important?

62
00:04:11,610 --> 00:04:14,280
<i>Don't keep talking about this.</i>

63
00:04:14,280 --> 00:04:18,620
I'm more on Team Better Do Than Don't.

64
00:04:14,570 --> 00:04:17,240
Nosebleed 
imminent...

65
00:04:14,570 --> 00:04:17,240
<i>Don't rub salt into my wounds!</i>

66
00:04:17,240 --> 00:04:21,200
<i>Gah! "Anything goes," my ass!</i>

67
00:04:17,530 --> 00:04:21,200
I never should've 
asked her if 
she felt sad!!

68
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:29,210
Let's put him down. Ready?

69
00:04:29,210 --> 00:04:33,280
Wait, gimme a sec. Okay.

70
00:04:40,130 --> 00:04:45,780
We should take him out before 
he revives and attacks any civilians.

71
00:04:40,430 --> 00:04:47,980
While he's still human

72
00:04:43,180 --> 00:04:47,980
What is he, a zombie?

73
00:04:45,780 --> 00:04:47,980
He might be having fun in his dreams.

74
00:04:48,290 --> 00:04:50,510
He must've had a lot on his mind.

75
00:04:50,510 --> 00:04:53,440
I'm not surprised, 
after how he kept drinking.

76
00:04:52,770 --> 00:04:54,110
You're partly to blame, too, girl

77
00:04:55,230 --> 00:04:57,570
Did he say anything about me?

78
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:57,570
Anything else

79
00:04:59,530 --> 00:05:01,680
Wouldn't you like to know?

80
00:05:00,070 --> 00:05:02,490
smirk

81
00:05:02,940 --> 00:05:06,790
I mean, I do feel bad 
for saying I'd "look into it."

82
00:05:06,790 --> 00:05:10,210
All I'm really doing is keeping him 
waiting, knowing how he feels.

83
00:05:12,970 --> 00:05:15,400
He said a buncha stuff.

84
00:05:15,400 --> 00:05:19,630
He went "blah this, blah that" for, like, 
two hours before you showed up.

85
00:05:20,200 --> 00:05:24,470
But if I sum it all up, all he really 
said was how much he loves you.

86
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:34,710
I'm sorry for making that 
inappropriate suggestion back there.

87
00:05:35,970 --> 00:05:39,400
This really only comes 
down to how you feel.

88
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:43,150
Master will wait as long as you want, 
be it three years or three billion.

89
00:05:43,070 --> 00:05:44,490
Even as a zombie

90
00:05:44,810 --> 00:05:48,490
I'm satisfied just knowing 
that the label's changed.

91
00:05:48,490 --> 00:05:49,200
Huh?

92
00:05:49,580 --> 00:05:52,500
You went from "I don't know" 
to "I miss having him around."

93
00:05:55,330 --> 00:05:57,920
Lemme go grab a taxi.

94
00:06:17,730 --> 00:06:19,780
You drank too much, dummy.

95
00:06:35,120 --> 00:06:39,090
Kissing him again 
should tell you something.

96
00:07:38,320 --> 00:07:39,230
...love you.

97
00:07:42,720 --> 00:07:45,070
I love you, Mizuhara...

98
00:07:59,230 --> 00:07:59,880
Huh?

99
00:08:00,230 --> 00:08:01,960
Wh-Whoa!

100
00:08:05,300 --> 00:08:07,750
Keep it together, will you?

101
00:08:07,750 --> 00:08:09,260
Mizuhara-san!

102
00:08:09,550 --> 00:08:12,220
A taxi

103
00:08:09,680 --> 00:08:12,220
One's coming over here.

104
00:08:14,780 --> 00:08:17,060
Huh? What were you doing?

105
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:22,810
Oh, nothing. He was about to fall over.

106
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:22,810
Just holding him up

107
00:08:22,860 --> 00:08:25,280
What an angel

108
00:08:23,510 --> 00:08:24,790
You're so nice.

109
00:08:26,240 --> 00:08:29,270
There it is. Over here!

110
00:08:29,740 --> 00:08:31,960
You good to go, Mizuhara-san?

111
00:08:31,960 --> 00:08:33,350
Yeah, I'm good.

112
00:08:33,350 --> 00:08:35,020
One, two, and...

113
00:08:35,020 --> 00:08:38,210
Man, he's heavy! 
Was he this heavy a minute ago?!

114
00:08:38,210 --> 00:08:42,170
C'mon, Master, help us out here!

115
00:08:50,380 --> 00:08:53,990
<i>I may have drunk a little too much myself.</i>

116
00:08:55,650 --> 00:08:57,000
I'll sit up front.

117
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:58,530
Oh, okay.

118
00:09:08,010 --> 00:09:10,440
You're going to Ekoda, right?

119
00:09:10,440 --> 00:09:11,570
That's right.

120
00:09:11,570 --> 00:09:12,530
Huh?

121
00:09:12,530 --> 00:09:14,280
Ekoda? Where in Ekoda?

122
00:09:14,780 --> 00:09:16,700
Your place, where else?

123
00:09:17,540 --> 00:09:20,040
Master looks like he's 
at the end of his rope.

124
00:09:17,740 --> 00:09:20,040
Not a moment
to waste

125
00:09:20,330 --> 00:09:21,500
This a boat...?

126
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:25,940
What the heck? I will not allow it!

127
00:09:38,450 --> 00:09:40,530
Oh, am I back in my apartment?

128
00:09:41,660 --> 00:09:45,330
Wait, what? I don't remember a thing!

129
00:09:41,690 --> 00:09:49,360
Did I do

130
00:09:41,690 --> 00:09:49,360
something stupid again?!

131
00:09:45,330 --> 00:09:49,360
I do recall drinking with Mizuhara, 
but what happened after that?

132
00:09:52,790 --> 00:09:53,860
Yes?

133
00:09:54,280 --> 00:09:57,370
Oh, long time no see, Kazuya-kun.

134
00:09:57,710 --> 00:09:59,750
Wha? Sayuri-san?

135
00:09:59,750 --> 00:10:01,050
What're you doing here?

136
00:10:01,050 --> 00:10:03,710
I stopped by on the way back 
from visiting Chizuru.

137
00:10:04,040 --> 00:10:07,930
I'm here to tell you something important.

138
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,670
Something
important?

139
00:10:07,930 --> 00:10:08,670
Huh?

140
00:10:08,670 --> 00:10:12,420
Well, I want you to stop seeing Chizuru.

141
00:10:12,740 --> 00:10:13,840
What?!

142
00:10:14,130 --> 00:10:15,900
Wh-Why?

143
00:10:15,900 --> 00:10:19,270
It seems she finished 
her... "investigation"?

144
00:10:19,620 --> 00:10:22,350
And she realized she 
doesn't like you one bit.

145
00:10:22,690 --> 00:10:24,650
Wha... No...

146
00:10:26,210 --> 00:10:29,490
Where's Chizuru-san? Let me talk to her!

147
00:10:29,490 --> 00:10:30,780
The thing is,

148
00:10:30,780 --> 00:10:34,660
KEEP OUT!
STAY AWAY!

149
00:10:30,780 --> 00:10:34,660
she asked me to tell you that she doesn't 
even want to see your face anymore.

150
00:10:37,120 --> 00:10:40,990
I'm sorry, Kazuya-kun. I'll send you 
year-end messages, at least.

151
00:10:43,460 --> 00:10:45,960
<i>N-No...</i>

152
00:10:46,460 --> 00:10:48,050
<i>No way...</i>

153
00:10:51,420 --> 00:10:52,970
This can't be!

154
00:11:00,590 --> 00:11:02,390
Wait, what?

155
00:11:02,790 --> 00:11:05,350
A pillow... and a bed? Was that a dream?

156
00:11:05,810 --> 00:11:09,510
What happened? I don't remember 
what happened after that drinking sesh.

157
00:11:09,400 --> 00:11:11,190
You're practically
replaying the same scene

158
00:11:11,470 --> 00:11:14,040
Wait, I recognize this place.

159
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:15,650
Oh, are you finally up?

160
00:11:20,480 --> 00:11:21,500
Good... day?

161
00:11:24,860 --> 00:11:28,290
<i>Mizuhara's place?!</i>

162
00:11:28,290 --> 00:11:29,060
Am I dreaming?

163
00:11:29,060 --> 00:11:31,980
What? Quit sleep-talking 
and wake up already.

164
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,000
Rent-a-Girlfriend

165
00:11:34,040 --> 00:11:36,220
Yaemori-san talked me into this.

166
00:11:36,640 --> 00:11:38,680
It got really late last night,

167
00:11:38,680 --> 00:11:43,380
and taking you home in that state 
would only worry your family.

168
00:11:46,420 --> 00:11:47,350
Are you listening?

169
00:11:50,120 --> 00:11:51,180
Hey, what?

170
00:11:57,800 --> 00:12:01,250
<i>What the heck? I'm sick as hell!</i>

171
00:12:01,250 --> 00:12:04,870
<i>I'm in this dream situation of 
waking up in Mizuhara's place,</i>

172
00:12:04,870 --> 00:12:07,410
<i>but I'm in no state to enjoy it!</i>

173
00:12:08,110 --> 00:12:09,880
Are you going to be okay?

174
00:12:10,160 --> 00:12:12,210
You were a mess last night, you know.

175
00:12:12,750 --> 00:12:17,670
It took all we both had
to get you here

176
00:12:12,810 --> 00:12:17,670
You wouldn't budge an inch, and it felt 
like you'd throw up any water we gave you.

177
00:12:17,670 --> 00:12:21,840
<i>Ugh, I made trouble for her yet again.</i>

178
00:12:17,970 --> 00:12:23,640
Always feels a lot older
the morning after drinking too much

179
00:12:21,840 --> 00:12:23,640
<i>What is wrong with me?</i>

180
00:12:23,640 --> 00:12:28,370
D-Don't you feel the least bit sad?

181
00:12:28,370 --> 00:12:32,360
<i>Now I'm just a nosy drunk 
who got completely plastered!</i>

182
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:35,110
Oh, is Master up?

183
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:36,370
<i>She warned me about this once already,</i>

184
00:12:35,110 --> 00:12:37,860
He's still living his nightmare, though.

185
00:12:36,370 --> 00:12:39,820
<i>but I just did the same thing 
again and had her look after me.</i>

186
00:12:37,860 --> 00:12:39,820
Not satisfied, eh?

187
00:12:40,110 --> 00:12:45,290
I never 
learn

188
00:12:40,120 --> 00:12:42,160
<i>I fail as a man.</i>

189
00:12:41,110 --> 00:12:45,290
The very image
of a failed man

190
00:12:42,160 --> 00:12:45,290
<i>The investigation concludes 
with me getting an F!</i>

191
00:12:42,870 --> 00:12:45,290
No walking 
this back

192
00:12:45,290 --> 00:12:48,500
I want you to stop seeing Chizuru.

193
00:12:48,500 --> 00:12:51,010
<i>That dream was prophetic.</i>

194
00:12:51,860 --> 00:12:55,060
<i>It's over! It's all over!</i>

195
00:12:52,690 --> 00:12:54,510
Just sit tight.

196
00:12:55,060 --> 00:12:57,470
Go ahead. Get it all out of your system.

197
00:12:58,400 --> 00:12:59,950
Yay.

198
00:13:03,940 --> 00:13:06,850
I love you, Mizuhara...

199
00:13:07,690 --> 00:13:08,630
Sheesh.

200
00:13:17,010 --> 00:13:18,840
You must be Kazuya-kun, right?

201
00:13:34,660 --> 00:13:36,080
I should die.

202
00:13:36,590 --> 00:13:39,420
<i>Nothing good will happen even if I live.</i>

203
00:13:39,420 --> 00:13:43,370
<i>Mizuhara will reject me and 
go off with some other guy.</i>

204
00:13:43,370 --> 00:13:46,420
<i>I wouldn't be able to 
bear seeing it happen.</i>

205
00:13:46,220 --> 00:13:50,520
Angel Sumi

206
00:13:46,420 --> 00:13:50,520
This pessimism is the 
acetaldehyde talking!

207
00:13:50,830 --> 00:13:55,980
<i>Getting that drunk was on me, too. 
I brought this upon myself.</i>

208
00:13:56,370 --> 00:14:03,390
<i>I'll never get a girl like that to 
seriously consider me an option again.</i>

209
00:14:08,700 --> 00:14:09,870
Mizuhara...!!

210
00:14:13,520 --> 00:14:15,540
Here, have some water.

211
00:14:16,030 --> 00:14:17,730
I-I'm sorry.

212
00:14:17,730 --> 00:14:19,750
<i>I don't know how to face her!</i>

213
00:14:22,720 --> 00:14:25,300
This hangover might last into tomorrow.

214
00:14:26,040 --> 00:14:27,770
I won't tell you not to drink,

215
00:14:27,770 --> 00:14:30,470
but drinking that much 
is just awful for you,

216
00:14:30,470 --> 00:14:34,560
and it's not good to make 
people worry about you.

217
00:14:34,560 --> 00:14:36,120
S-Sorry.

218
00:14:35,480 --> 00:14:43,030
It just keeps
piling up

219
00:14:36,120 --> 00:14:39,170
<i>Ugh, she is so done with me.</i>

220
00:14:39,170 --> 00:14:41,320
<i>But wait, what's she doing here?</i>

221
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:42,190
Hey.

222
00:14:43,460 --> 00:14:45,410
Are you feeling good enough for a chat?

223
00:14:44,570 --> 00:14:45,410
You can 
stay there

224
00:14:46,780 --> 00:14:48,330
<i>H-Here it comes!</i>

225
00:14:48,850 --> 00:14:51,740
<i>It's all over. She's going to announce 
the end of her investigation.</i>

226
00:14:51,740 --> 00:14:55,880
<i>Trust Mizuhara to try and do 
things as promptly as possible!</i>

227
00:14:53,370 --> 00:14:56,290
Here and now

228
00:14:56,670 --> 00:14:58,520
Mini-chan told me...

229
00:14:58,520 --> 00:15:02,630
you can't find a place until next month, 
and you feel awkward at home.

230
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:06,340
<i>She knows about that, too? 
I feel pathetic!</i>

231
00:15:07,010 --> 00:15:08,760
<i>Is it all coming to an end now?</i>

232
00:15:08,760 --> 00:15:12,600
<i>Our past, present, and future 
are just going to get vaporized?</i>

233
00:15:12,600 --> 00:15:15,440
<i>No! I don't wanna hear it!</i>

234
00:15:15,770 --> 00:15:17,120
<i>I should leave.</i>

235
00:15:15,980 --> 00:15:18,940
Before she rejects me

236
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:18,940
I-I'll be fine!

237
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:26,280
I-I found capsule hotels 
for 3,000 yen a night,

238
00:15:26,280 --> 00:15:30,960
and I'm sure Kibe and Kuri will 
let me stay a few days, at least.

239
00:15:26,450 --> 00:15:33,120
And I have the 
moving-out fee!

240
00:15:30,960 --> 00:15:33,120
It's just a month. I'll manage somehow.

241
00:15:33,650 --> 00:15:37,030
Don't worry about me. You can just...

242
00:15:45,800 --> 00:15:48,130
You need to stay in bed and recover.

243
00:15:49,270 --> 00:15:52,470
But I can't stay here two nights in a row.

244
00:15:55,650 --> 00:15:57,350
Just one month.

245
00:15:59,890 --> 00:16:00,770
Huh?

246
00:16:07,930 --> 00:16:10,600
I'm only letting you use 
this room and nothing else.

247
00:16:10,600 --> 00:16:13,090
We'll have to share the bathroom,

248
00:16:13,090 --> 00:16:15,410
but otherwise we'll maintain 
separate spaces,

249
00:16:15,410 --> 00:16:19,080
And laundry
stays separate

250
00:16:15,410 --> 00:16:17,420
and you have to help clean the place.

251
00:16:18,160 --> 00:16:19,080
Also...

252
00:16:19,570 --> 00:16:21,380
You have to stay here, too, Yaemori-san.

253
00:16:19,620 --> 00:16:21,080
She's here

254
00:16:21,250 --> 00:16:25,420
